 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? That's really common. When you stop and move around, your brain actually comes back online more quickly. Take short walk around the block, then come back. Usually the focus returns on its own. Stand up, stretch, and do something that reaches different parts of your body. It also helps change your environment a little, like moving to a different spot. Exactly. Checking email or social media in same seat can just keep you there. And don't beat yourself up about it. Taking breaks actually helps with focus.",
